    "content": "The North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO) is a political and military alliance established in 1949 to guarantee the freedom and security of its members through collective defense. Comprising 32 countries from Europe and North America, its core principle, Article 5, dictates that an attack against one member is an attack against all. Key Aspects of NATO: Collective Defense (Article 5): The foundation of the alliance, promising mutual aid if a member is attacked. Purpose: Founded to deter Soviet expansionism after WWII; it now addresses modern security threats, including terrorism and regional instability. Members: As of 2024, there are 32 member countries, including the U.S., Canada, and most of Europe. Funding & Spending: Members commit to investing in their own defense, with a target of 5% of GDP annually on defence and security-related spending by 2035. Headquarters: The political headquarters are located in Brussels, Belgium. NATO operates on the principle that its members are safer together, with a combined defense force that represents the largest in the world.",
